IIRC, in nethack you have a to-hit bonus of 1/level (that is, in D&D
terms, your BAB is equal to your level) whatever your role. In D&D, your
BAB may be either your level, 3/4 of your level or 1/2 your level.
So, twoweaponing for D&D wizards is not too powerfull because the maluses
(to the attack roll and of the feats you need to take) are rather big. In
nethack, the maluses are too small and thus a twoweaponing wizard would be
too powerfull.

Of course, the DevTeam could have choose to diferenciate the BAB's groth
rather than the twoweaponing ability. This is probably what you call
"fixing things that should be".

